[38;5;231m⏺[39m Fixed the off-by-one in [38;5;153msrc/textkit/chunking.py:18[39m.

  [1mRoot cause:[0m [38;5;153mtext[i:i + chunk_size - 1][39m — Python slice ends are exclusive, so the extra [38;5;153m- 1[39m truncated every chunk to
  [38;5;153mchunk_size - 1[39m characters and silently dropped the character at each boundary. The loop step was already correct at
  [38;5;153mchunk_size[39m, so the dropped characters never reappeared in any chunk.

  [1mFix:[0m [38;5;153mtext[i:i + chunk_size][39m.

  Why the existing tests only caught it partially: the three passing cases ([38;5;153m"hi"[39m with size 10, [38;5;153m""[39m, and the [38;5;153mValueError[39m
  cases) never exercise a boundary where the truncation is observable — with [38;5;153mchunk_size[39m larger than the text, the slice
  end still runs past the end of the string.

  [1mVerified:[0m
  - [38;5;153m.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q[39m — 2 failed before the change, 6 passed after.
  - [38;5;153mruff check[39m and [38;5;153mmypy[39m on the changed file — both clean.

